# Trivy ignore list (image scans).
# Each entry MUST include: severity, justification, expiry-or-followup.
# Re-evaluate every time we bump caddy / dependencies.
#
# How to re-audit (no docker needed): read the dependency versions caddy pins
# in its own go.mod for the tag we build —
#   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/caddyserver/caddy/<CADDY_VERSION>/go.mod
# — then ask OSV whether that exact version is still affected:
#   POST https://api.osv.dev/v1/query {"package":{"name":"<mod>","ecosystem":"Go"},"version":"<ver>"}
# An empty result means caddy has moved past the fix and the entry below is
# dead weight; delete it. OSV and trivy's DB are not identical, so confirm on
# the next CI run — the docker-images job scans with exit-code 0 and prints the
# full HIGH/CRITICAL table.

# === caddy gobinary, frontend + panel images ==================================
#
# Caddy v2.11.4 binary embeds these third-party libs at the versions caddy's
# go.mod pinned. The vulnerable code paths are NOT reachable in our
# `frontend/Caddyfile.panel`:
#
#   * `auto_https off` — no ACME / no internal CA / no smallstep SCEP;
#   * no Caddy OTel telemetry exporter enabled;
#   * no gRPC reverse-proxy modules;
#   * no ACME-DNS challenge and no custom `resolvers` — x/net dnsmessage
#     wire-parsing not exercised;
#   * static `file_server` + HTTP `reverse_proxy` only — no language matchers
#     or x/text encoding on the request path.
#
# Caddy upstream ships these libs in their binary regardless of whether the
# affected modules are loaded; we accept the trivy noise until caddy releases a
# binary built against patched deps. v2.11.4 (2026-06-03) is still the newest
# release as of 2026-09-04, so none of the five below can be cleared yet.
# Followup: bump caddy on every upstream release, then re-run the audit above.

CVE-2026-46600        # HIGH x/net v0.55.0 — dnsmessage DoS; no ACME-DNS / no custom resolvers, DNS wire-parsing unreachable.
CVE-2026-56852        # HIGH x/text v0.37.0 — UTF-8 DoS; no language matchers / x/text encoding on static+proxy request path.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf   # HIGH grpc-go v1.81.0 (fix 1.82.1) — xDS RBAC + HTTP/2; no gRPC modules, caddy HTTP/2 server is x/net/http2, not grpc-go.
CVE-2026-56854        # CRITICAL x/crypto v0.52.0 (fix 0.55.0) — flaw is in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh; caddy standard build has no SSH server or client module, x/crypto is linked for TLS/ACME only.
CVE-2026-84304        # HIGH grpc-go v1.81.0 (fix 1.83.1) — caddy gRPC modules not loaded; panel serves static files + HTTP reverse_proxy only. Our own backend already runs grpc v1.83.2.
